---
import Doc from '../_Doc.astro'
import { categories, statusValues } from '../../../lib/extensions-docs.js'

const cats = categories()
const STEPS = `# 0. Preconditions: a clone of mbaliga/asystemofcells, Node 18+. No npm packages are needed for the SDK.
# 1. Scaffold (templates: hello | theme). The id is permanent: choose it once.
node extensions/sdk/create.mjs hello extensions/clackpad/my-ext --id io.github.<owner>.<name> --author "<Author>"
# 2. Edit extensions/clackpad/my-ext/extension.json, README.md, CHANGELOG.md, LICENSE, NOTICE.md
# 3. Validate the folder (exit 0 = valid)
node extensions/sdk/validate.mjs extensions/clackpad/my-ext
# 4. Add one entry to extensions/clackpad/catalog.json (see below)
# 5. Build everything (writes dist/, index.json, store.json)
node extensions/tools/build.mjs clackpad
# 6. Prove nothing is stale (exit 0 = up to date)
node extensions/tools/build.mjs clackpad --check
# 7. Open ONE pull request containing only this extension`
const ENTRY = `{ "dir": "my-ext", "status": "community", "noncommercial": true, "category": "productivity", "tags": ["notes"], "screenshots": [] }`
const PASS = `$ node extensions/sdk/validate.mjs extensions/clackpad/my-ext
OK  extensions/clackpad/my-ext

$ node extensions/sdk/pack.mjs my-ext my-ext.cpx
my-ext.cpx  1890 bytes
sha256 <64 hex chars>

$ node extensions/tools/build.mjs clackpad --check
my-ext: <id>-<version>.cpx  <bytes> bytes  sha256 <64 hex chars>
OK  dist/, index.json and store.json are up to date`
const FAIL = `$ node extensions/sdk/validate.mjs my-ext
3 problems in my-ext:
  - bogus: unknown key
  - permissions[0]: unknown permission "bogus"
  - contributes.action[0]: {{typed}} needs the "typed:read" permission`
---
<Doc
  title="For AI agents"
  description="A precise, machine-friendly guide for AI coding agents building and submitting Clackpad extensions: exact commands, file layout, what a passing run prints, common failures, hard limits, and the machine-readable endpoints."
  path="/extensions/agents/"
  eyebrow="Extensions / Agents"
  heading="Extensions: guide for AI coding agents"
  lead="Follow the steps in order. Everything here is checkable by a command; if a command fails, fix the cause, never the check."
  sources={['extensions/sdk/validate.mjs', 'extensions/tools/build.mjs', 'extensions/sdk/schemas/extension.schema.json']}
>
  <h2 id="endpoints">Machine-readable endpoints</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Machine-readable endpoints">
    <table class="dense-table">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">URL</th><th scope="col">What</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><a href="/llms.txt"><code>https://asystemofcells.dev/llms.txt</code></a></td><td>Concise map of these docs and the rules</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/extensions/schemas/extension.schema.json"><code>/extensions/schemas/extension.schema.json</code></a></td><td>JSON Schema of <code>extension.json</code> (editor aid; the validator is authoritative)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/extensions/schemas/catalog.schema.json"><code>/extensions/schemas/catalog.schema.json</code></a></td><td>JSON Schema of a catalog index entry</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/extensions/permissions.json"><code>/extensions/permissions.json</code></a></td><td>Permission ids, labels, risk and meaning</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>The three JSON files are generated at build time from the repository files named on each page, so they match the repository at the commit the site was built from.</p>

  <h2 id="steps">Steps and exact commands</h2>
  <pre><code>{STEPS}</code></pre>
  <p>The <code>catalog.json</code> entry (add it to the <code>extensions</code> array; the other fields come from <code>extension.json</code>):</p>
  <pre><code>{ENTRY}</code></pre>
  <p><code>category</code> must be one of: {cats.map((c, i) => (<>{i > 0 ? ', ' : ''}<code>{c}</code></>))}. <code>status</code> is set by maintainers: propose <code>community</code> (or <code>fan-made</code> with <code>"noncommercial": true</code> for imitation work) and expect review to decide.</p>

  <h2 id="layout">File layout</h2>
  <pre><code>extensions/clackpad/
  catalog.json            you edit: add one entry
  index.json  store.json  generated by build.mjs: commit, never hand-edit
  dist/                   generated: commit; never delete older .cpx files
  my-ext/
    extension.json        schema clackpad-extension/1
    icon.png              PNG, at most 64 KB
    README.md  LICENSE  NOTICE.md  CHANGELOG.md
    pages/ themes/        only if used</code></pre>

  <h2 id="passing">What a passing run prints</h2>
  <pre><code>{PASS}</code></pre>
  <p>The validator exits 0 when valid, 1 with errors, 2 on usage errors. <code>validate.mjs --json</code> gives machine-readable output; <code>--host-version N</code> checks against build <code>N</code>.</p>

  <h2 id="failures">Common failures and fixes</h2>
  <pre><code>{FAIL}</code></pre>
  <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Common failures">
    <table class="dense-table">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Message</th><th scope="col">Fix</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>&lt;key&gt;: unknown key</code></td><td>Remove it. Manifest objects reject unknown keys. See <a href="/extensions/format/">Manifest format</a>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>unknown permission "x"</code></td><td>Use only ids from <a href="/extensions/permissions.json">permissions.json</a>. Do not invent permissions.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>{'{{typed}}'} needs the "typed:read" permission</code></td><td>Either declare the permission the template needs, with a justification in the PR, or remove the variable. Do not add permissions that nothing uses.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>id:</code> errors from <code>create.mjs</code></td><td>The id must match <code>^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*(\.[a-z][a-z0-9-]*)+$</code>, max 64 chars, at least two segments.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>&lt;dir&gt; already exists and is not empty</code></td><td>Pick a new folder; never scaffold over existing work.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>catalog.json needs "category", one of ...</code></td><td>Set <code>category</code> to a value in the list above.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>screenshot &lt;path&gt; does not exist</code></td><td>Paths are relative to the app folder (<code>extensions/clackpad/</code>). Add the file or remove the entry.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dist/&lt;file&gt; is out of date</code> / <code>index.json is out of date</code> / <code>store.json is out of date</code></td><td>Run <code>node extensions/tools/build.mjs clackpad</code> (without <code>--check</code>) and commit the result. The message mentions <code>./build.sh</code>; in this repository the command is the <code>build.mjs</code> one.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>no catalog.json in ...</code> (exit 2)</td><td>Pass the app folder name: <code>clackpad</code>.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="must-not">What an agent must NOT do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Do not invent permissions</b> or declare any that nothing in the manifest uses. The schema pattern and <a href="/extensions/permissions.json">permissions.json</a> are the full list.</li>
    <li><b>Do not bundle third-party IP</b>: no trademarks, logos, fonts, sounds, dictionaries or code you cannot redistribute. Draw icons from scratch. State the <code>license</code> and ship the licence text.</li>
    <li><b>Do not reuse a version number with different bytes.</b> Bump <code>version</code>, add a <code>CHANGELOG.md</code> line, rebuild. Never delete older <code>.cpx</code> files from <code>dist/</code>.</li>
    <li><b>Do not bypass review.</b> One extension per pull request. Do not hand-edit <code>index.json</code>, <code>store.json</code> or <code>dist/</code>; do not weaken or skip <code>--check</code>; do not set <code>status: official</code>.</li>
    <li><b>Do not claim facts you did not observe.</b> Do not write that something was tested on a device, or invent install counts, ratings or reviews: there is no telemetry.</li>
    <li><b>Do not imply affiliation</b> with a company whose product an extension works with. Say it is unaffiliated.</li>
    <li><b>Do not pick an id carelessly.</b> It is permanent and names the install folder and the page origin.</li>
    <li><b>Do not put code in the keyboard.</b> There is none: packages with <code>.dex .so .apk .jar</code> and similar are refused. Page scripts go in <code>.js</code> files; inline scripts are blocked.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="tools">Related tools</h2>
  <p>
    The scaffold CLI is <code>extensions/sdk/create.mjs</code>. The in-browser <b>Extension Studio</b> is <b>planned to move here</b>; it is not available on this site yet, and agents should use the CLI.
  </p>
</Doc>
